From 1ac8ef7d89011e5e0c9b607b9c0f1efa650e00f9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hardening <hardening@example.invalid>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 10:03:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/9] build: pin and verify every downloaded tool, run the
 container unprivileged

Local fork hardening, no upstream behaviour changes:

- nuclei/httpx/subfinder/katana/ffuf/dalfox: SHA-256 of the release archive is
  pinned per architecture and checked before install, so a replaced upstream
  asset fails the build instead of being installed silently.
- sqlmap: pinned to commit 397a3bd instead of cloning a moving branch, and the
  checkout is verified after fetch.
- Node 22 is copied from the pinned node:22-bookworm-slim build stage instead of
  piping deb.nodesource.com/setup_22.x into bash as root.
- Playwright MCP/CLI/playwright pinned to exact versions instead of @latest.
- Runtime image runs as uid 10001; /app/artex and /app/skills stay root-owned and
  read-only, only /app/data and /app/keys are writable.

Adds HARDENING.md (provenance evidence + maintenance notes) and
scripts/verify-provenance.sh, which re-checks the upstream commit against the Go
module proxy and a release asset against its SHA256SUMS and embedded buildinfo.

Not built here (no Docker in this environment); hashes were validated against
each vendor's published checksums file.
